        <localActions>
            <fullName>Candidate_Search_179g7000002D4eC</fullName>
            <description>Searches processed candidates by name, skill, minimum years of experience or location, without AI. Use it when the recruiter asks to find, list or filter candidates, for example &quot;find candidates with at least 10 years&quot; or &quot;who knows LWC in Madrid&quot;. Leave a filter empty to ignore it. Do not use it to compare candidates against a role. Returns a list with each candidate&apos;s name, Id, years, title and location, or a message when nobody matches.</description>
            <developerName>Candidate_Search_179g7000002D4eC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>Candidate_Search</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>flow</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>true</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Candidate_Search</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Search Candidates</masterLabel>
            <progressIndicatorMessage>Searching candidates</progressIndicatorMessage>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>evaluate_candidate_179g7000002D4eC</fullName>
            <description>Evaluates one or more candidates against one job role, ranks them by score and saves one evaluation per candidate. Use it when the recruiter asks to score, rank, compare or shortlist candidates, or asks who is the best fit for a role. Pass the role name and, if the recruiter gave any, all candidate names in one call, separated by commas (up to 10). With no candidate named, it evaluates the 5 most recent processed candidates. Returns a ranked list with each candidate&apos;s score, recommendation, confidence, points, strengths, gaps and risks, and says when no candidate is a strong match. If the role or a candidate is unclear, it returns a question to ask the recruiter.</description>
            <developerName>evaluate_candidate_179g7000002D4eC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>Evaluate_Candidates</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>flow</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>true</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>evaluate_candidate</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Evaluate Candidates</masterLabel>
            <progressIndicatorMessage>Evaluating candidates, this can take a moment</progressIndicatorMessage>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>Bookmark_candidate_179g7000002D4eC</fullName>
            <description>Saves a bookmark for a candidate who was already evaluated for a role, with the recruiter&apos;s notes. Use it only when the recruiter asks to bookmark, save or keep a candidate. Pass the candidate name, and the role name if more than one role was discussed; if the evaluation number is known (for example EVAL-00003), pass it instead. It copies the candidate overview, score, reasoning, role and date into one bookmark. If the candidate was not evaluated yet, or the name or role is unclear, it returns a question to ask the recruiter. If the candidate is already bookmarked for that evaluation, it says so and does not create a duplicate.</description>
            <developerName>Bookmark_candidate_179g7000002D4eC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>Bookmark_Candidate</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>flow</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>true</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Bookmark_candidate</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Bookmark Candidate</masterLabel>
            <progressIndicatorMessage>Saving the bookmark</progressIndicatorMessage>
        </localActions>
